@startuml SEQ_03_Student_Accept
title Sequence 3 — Student Accept (Atomic First-to-Accept)

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFCC
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #888

actor       "Student A"             as SA
actor       "Student B"             as SB
participant "Mobile App"            as App
participant "TaskAPI\n/tasks/"      as API
participant "DB Transaction"        as TX
participant "Task Model"            as TM
participant "TaskRequest Model"     as TR
participant "NotificationService"   as NS
database    "PostgreSQL"            as DB

== Student Views Inbox ==

SA  -> App : Open job requests inbox
App -> API : GET /tasks/my-requests/
API -> DB  : SELECT TaskRequest\nWHERE student=SA AND status=SENT
DB --> API : [request list]
API --> App : 200 OK {requests}
App --> SA  : Show request cards

SA  -> App : Tap "Accept" on request (request_id=R)

== Atomic Accept Transaction ==

App -> API : POST /tasks/accept-request/\n{request_id: R}

API -> TX  : BEGIN TRANSACTION (atomic)

TX  -> DB  : SELECT tasks_task\nWHERE id=T\nFOR UPDATE          /' row-level lock '/
DB --> TX  : task row (locked)

TX  -> DB  : SELECT tasks_taskrequest\nWHERE id=R\nFOR UPDATE
DB --> TX  : request row (locked)

alt Task status ≠ Broadcasting
  TX  -> TX  : ROLLBACK
  API --> App : 409 Conflict\n{"detail": "Task no longer available"}
  App --> SA  : "Sorry, this task was taken"

else Task.status == Broadcasting

  alt TaskRequest.status ≠ SENT (already TAKEN/EXPIRED)
    TX  -> TX  : ROLLBACK
    API --> App : 409 Conflict\n{"detail": "Request already processed"}
    App --> SA  : "Request no longer active"

  else Request is SENT and task is Broadcasting

    TX  -> TR  : request.status = ACCEPTED\nrequest.responded_at = now()
    TR  -> DB  : UPDATE tasks_taskrequest SET status='ACCEPTED'

    TX  -> DB  : UPDATE tasks_taskrequest\nSET status='TAKEN'\nWHERE task=T\nAND student ≠ SA\nAND status IN (SENT, VIEWED)
    note right : All other pending requests\nmarked TAKEN atomically

    TX  -> TM  : task.status = Matched\ntask.assigned_student = SA\ntask.grace_window_deadline\n  = now() + 10 min
    TM  -> DB  : UPDATE tasks_task\nSET status='Matched',\nassigned_student=SA,\ngrace_window_deadline=…

    TX  -> TX  : COMMIT

    API -> NS  : send(\n  recipient=SA,\n  type=TASK_MATCHED,\n  title="You got the job!",\n  task_id=T\n)
    NS  -> DB  : INSERT notification (SA)

    API -> NS  : send(\n  recipient=HH,\n  type=TASK_MATCHED,\n  title="Student matched – confirm within 10 min",\n  task_id=T\n)
    NS  -> DB  : INSERT notification (HH)

    API --> App : 200 OK\n{task_id, matched_student,\ngrace_window_deadline}
    App --> SA  : "You matched! Waiting for household to confirm."
  end
end

== Concurrent Accept Attempt (Student B loses the race) ==

note over SB, DB
  Student B taps Accept on the same task at nearly the same time.
  The SELECT … FOR UPDATE blocks until Student A's transaction commits.
  By the time B's lock is granted, task.status = Matched → 409 returned.
end note

SB  -> App : POST /tasks/accept-request/ {request_id: R2}
App -> API : (arrives while A's TX is in-flight or just committed)
API -> TX  : BEGIN TRANSACTION
TX  -> DB  : SELECT tasks_task WHERE id=T FOR UPDATE
DB --> TX  : task (status=Matched)
TX  -> TX  : ROLLBACK — status ≠ Broadcasting
API --> App : 409 Conflict
App --> SB  : "Task no longer available"

@enduml
